# Pokemon Crystal LIVE link trade, guest side: starts from a running game
# (the gen2_counter_guest.ap end state, standing at the Cable Trade Center
# receptionist) -- no boot, no restart.  The host disconnects after the
# trade (the menu's Disconnect); both then play on.
hold UP 8
wait 20
# YES, wait for the friend, save, and walk in (map 20:2 TRADE_CENTER)
mash A 1 0xDCB6 0xFF 2 4000
evt in_trade_center
wait 120
# --- the internal-clock side sits at (3,4) facing right, the other at
# (6,4) facing left (TradeCenter.asm; hSerialConnectionStatus $FFCB = 2)
stepram UP 1 0xDCB7 0xFF 5 1000
ifram 1 0xFFCB 0xFF 2 3
stepram LEFT 1 0xDCB8 0xFF 3 1000
stepram UP 1 0xDCB7 0xFF 4 1000
hold RIGHT 8
ifram 1 0xFFCB 0xFF 1 3
stepram RIGHT 1 0xDCB8 0xFF 6 1000
stepram UP 1 0xDCB7 0xFF 4 1000
hold LEFT 8
wait 20
logbytes seat 2 0xDCB7
hold A 6
wait 800
# --- our third Pokemon (SANDSHREW "GIFTSHREW"): TRADE, confirm
hold DOWN 6
wait 30
hold DOWN 6
wait 30
hold A 6
wait 60
hold RIGHT 6
wait 30
hold A 6
wait 400
mash A 1 0xDCDA 0xFF 0x3F 4000
evt traded
# The games save by themselves once the trade animation ends (~90 s).
# Not waitsram: both use cartridge RAM as scratch for Pokemon pictures, so
# its CRC moves long before the save lands.  score_trade.py judges the save.
wait 5400
evt settled
logbytes party 7 0xDCD7
# --- the session ends a margin later; then the game plays on from where it
# stands (no restart): still in the Trade Center (map 20:2), taking input.
wait 900
evt resumed
waitram 1 0xDCB5 0xFF 20 60
waitram 1 0xDCB6 0xFF 2 60
hold UP 8
wait 60
logbytes pos 4 0xDCB5
evt played_on
